Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA  Extensive ductal carcinoma in situ with microinvasion in the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  ONE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 21 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The margins of the mastectomy specimen appear free of invasive carcinoma  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The lymph node metastasis spans less than 0 2cm and does not transgress the lymph node capsule    RIGHT BREAST TISSUE    UNREMARKABLE SKIN AND FAT  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT MASTECTOMY   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a single mass containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail attached to a breast of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin flap and inverted nipple with a 3 0cm scar on the skin flap on the opposite side from the axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm gray area beneath the incisional scar containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hollow cavity and several 0 1cm nodules in the adjacent fat  Representative sections of the cavity are submitted in A through D  with E containing the closest margin  The specimen also contains other gray areas  representative sections are submitted in F through H  Lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes I through L  from distal to proximal  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue flap  are multiple fragments of adipose tissue and strips of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm in aggregate  representative sections are submitted in M and N  Gross Description by  ANTHONY FORRESTER  HMS Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  G  Gregory Gallico I