Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 02 CLINICAL DATA  45 year old female with a history of a 4 0cm left breast carcinoma  Recent biopsy showed a possible positive margin  The patient now presents for a a re excision and axillary node dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 3 3   PRESENT WITHIN LYMPHATICS AND METASTATIC TO 14 OF 26 LYMPH NODES  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The residual carcinoma is present in lymphatics away from the biopsy site and is immediately adjacent to the medial resection margin  There is focal extracapsular extension of the carcinoma in some of the lymph nodes  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 06                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm skin ellipse  that contains a centrally located  longitudinal  5 5cm  well healed surgical incision  The lobectomy specimen has a long stitch in place designating the lateral margin and a short stitch designating the medial margin  The specimen is inked in black on the lateral half and inked in yellow on the medial half  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  blood filled biopsy cavity with yellow streaks and firm ragged edges  located 0 2cm from the deep resection margin  The biopsy cavity is 3 5cm from superior margin  1 5cm from the inferior margin  3 0cm from the lateral margin  3 5cm from the medial margin and 0 3cm subadjacent to the anterior overlying skin ellipse  The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable and is composed of white  smooth  rubbery breast tissue with a few areas of yellow  soft  lobulated fat  SECTION CODE  A  inferior margin  radial section B  deep margin with cavity  radial section C  superior margin  radial section D  lateral margin  en face E  medial margin  en face F  anterior margin  skin with cavity G K  biopsy cavity  representative sections L N  breast parenchyma  representative sections Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two separate parts  Labeled  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of yellow red  fibrofatty breast tissue with multiple  firm  palpable lymph nodes  The specimen is dissected to reveal twenty lymph nodes which range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 4cm in greatest dimension and have cut surfaces that range from fleshy tan to soft yellow to speckled yellow  The smaller nodes are submitted entirely  while one representative section of the larger nodes is submitted  O V  lymph nodes  left axilla  Labeled  additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is bisected to reveal THREE lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 6cm in greatest dimension  having a fleshy tan to homogeneously white and firm cut surface  One half of the entire sample is submitted in W  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  COMPLETELY EXCISED BIOPSY CAVITY COMING WITHIN 0 2CM OF DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
