Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 39 CLINICAL DATA  Carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MICROSCOPIC FOCI ADJACENT TO ONE BIOPSY CAVITY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY CAVITIES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The results of immunohistochemical staining for keratin will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT   INFERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 98 at 15 35                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   The lymph nodes do not contain keratin positive carcinoma cells  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 98 at 14 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen  with attached axillary tissue  an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm skin ellipse  with a grossly unremarkable nipple at the inferior border  a 3 5cm well healed scar  1 0cm lateral to the nipple  and second well healed 3 5cm scar  5 5cm superior from the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity filled with red brown grumous material  located 3 0cm from the closest inked deep margin  1 5cm from the closest superior inked border  and 3 0cm deep to the overlying skin  A second biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm is located 3 0cm inferior to the first biopsy cavity  2 5cm from the closest deep inked margin  and 4 0cm deep to the overlying skin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavities is remarkable for areas of fat necrosis  white fibrous tissue  and more ill defined firm  focally gritty tissue that comes to within 4 5cm of the closest deep margin  2 5cm deep to the overlying skin and to within 2 5cm of the closest anterior inked resection margin  Approximately 1 0cm deep to the more superiorly located scar is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ill defined  firm area which comes to within 1 0cm of the closest superior inked margin and 2 0cm from the closest deep inked margin  No other discrete lesion is identified inferior to the scar  Approximately 1 5cm deep to the more inferiorly located scar is an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm area with central hemorrhage  5 5cm from the deep inked margin  and 2 5cm from the closest inferior inked resection margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma away from the biopsy cavities is composed of fibrofatty tissue  Sectioning through the axillary tail reveals multiple tan lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 1 5cm  is identified  Also submitted with the specimen is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal multiple tan lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  A D  Representative sections of more superiorly located biopsy cavity  E   Closest inked deep margin  to the first biopsy cavity   F I  Representative sections of the more inferiorly located biopsy cavity  J   Closest inked deep margin  in relation to second biopsy cavity   K N  Representative sections of more fibrous  firm  gritty areas adjacent to biopsy cavities  O   More ill defined  firm area inferior to the superiorly located scar  P   More ill defined  firm area  entirely submitted  deep to the more inferiorly located scar  Q U  Nodes from axillary tail  including lymph nodes from additional breast tissue submitted with the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left inferior breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue with no lymph nodes grossly identified  The tissue is submitted entirely in Cassettes W CC  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT INFERIOR   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 43 CLINICAL DATA  History of mother with breast cancer  Mammogram with new abnormality in central portion of the right breast  FNA was non diagnostic  Now presents for excisional breast biopsy  On physical exam no palpable masses in either breast and no adenopathy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    MODERATELY TO FOCALLY POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  ABOUT 1 CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  30    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  SEE NOTE   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported on in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 32     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm semifirm  tan yellow breast biopsy with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white  poorly circumscribed lesion  1 0cm in greatest dimension  grossly abutting an inked resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is notable for a mixture of white fibrous tissue and soft yellow adipose tissue  Representative section of lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the lesion is in A through E  remainder of specimen in F through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Yes.
