Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma  left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE 1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Four nodules  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  see note   Grade  REMOVED_DATE Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified Blood vessel invasion  Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater for all nodules Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within the region of the masses Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  2 Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater Stains for receptors  Requested NOTE  The four masses are located in both the medial and lateral aspects of the breast and are physically separated by upwards of 6cm  Despite this significant distance between four masses  all four masses have a highly similar histomorphology appearance  This latter finding favors multifocal rather than multicentric disease  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 31                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block C   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block G   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block I   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block K   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm irregular yellow rubbery lymph node which is bivalved and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast stitch as 12   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 4cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch denoting the superior margin  There is a central overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm circular portion of skin which contains a 3 1cm nipple areolar complex which is grossly unremarkable  The margins of resection are marked with black inked  The specimen is serially sectioned at 5mm intervals from medial to lateral  Four distinct lesions are identified and are described below in a medial to lateral fashion  Lesion  1  most medial  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and extends 1 8cm of the deep margin and 1 7cm of the anterior superior margin  Lesion  2  medial  is located 1cm lateral to lesion  1 and is ill defined mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The lesion extends to 3 5cm of the deep margin and 0 3cm of the anterior superior margin  Lesion  3  central  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and is located in the superior central portion of the breast and extends to 3 8cm of the deep margin to approximately 2cm of the anterior margin  The lesion is located approximately 6cm lateral to lesion  2  Lesion  2 3 have blue dye adjacent to them  Lesion  4 is  most lateral  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is located 2 0cm from the deep margin and 4 3cm from the anterior margin  The 4th lesion is located approximately 4 5cm lateral to the largest lesion   lesion  3   The remainder of the tissue consists predominately of adipose tissue with a few foci of soft white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  B D  Lesion  1  E G  Lesion  2  H I  Lesion  3  J  Shave margin  deep margin beneath lesion  3  K L  Lesion  4  M N  Sections of fibrous tissue between the different lesions  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  BIOPSY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No.
