es to 0 9cm from the superior  1 0cm from the inferior  2 0cm from the posterior  1 9cm from the medial and 2 7cm from the lateral margin  respectively  The cavity borders are tan yellow and rubbery with focal areas of fat necrosis  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow  lobulated and unremarkable with no discrete masses or lesions identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire previous biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Surrounding uninvolved parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node primary 82   is a lobulated tan pink rubbery potential lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned  and entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node secondary 25   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan pink rubbery potential lymph node which is submitted in toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by John H Eichhorn M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL  82   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL 25   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 53 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast core biopsy  eight core samples obtained                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  are eight fragments of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Joyce Nath  M D  Jaime L Kline  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  CORE BIOPSY , Unchecked.
