ors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 4cm portion of oriented breast tissue  A short suture designates the superficial margin  long and short sutures the inferior margin  and two long sutures the medial margin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with surrounding hard  white tissue  highly suspicious for tumor measuring 3 7cm in greatest dimension  radiating up to 0 8cm from the edge of the biopsy cavity  and approaching the superomedial and posteromedial margins  A second suspicious area  distant from the first area  measures 1 7cm in greatest dimension and approaches the superior margin of the specimen  SECTION CODE  A  Medial most section  B D  Closest superior margin  E F  Second lesion at superior margins  G   Representative section of superficial margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Part II   Final Inferior Margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast tissue  which is inked black  The inferior and deep margins are over inked blue  which had been previously designated by two stitches  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal cystification  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm gritty nodule  which comes within 0 3cm of the closest infero deep margin  inked blue   The gritty nodule is entirely submitted in Cassette H  Representative sections of cystification and adjacent unremarkable parenchyma are submitted in Cassettes I K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   3   final medial superior margin  short suture medial  long superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short suture designating the medial aspect  and a long suture on the superior margin  The superior margin is inked black  the inferior blue  There is a small amount of attached muscle on the deep margin  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a focally gritty fibrous area in the lateral half  measuring 0 5cm in greatest dimension  which abuts the inferior portion of the specimen  This gritty area is submitted entirely in Cassettes L M  The remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted from lateral to medial in Cassettes N X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  ranging from 0 3cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  A representative section of each is submitted in Cassettes Y CC  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   RE EXCISION RIGHT BREAST   INVASIVE CARCINOMA GROSSLY APPROACHING THE SUPERIOR  MEDIAL  AND POSTERIOMEDIAL INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UN