Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  19 MAY 04 at 15 21 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old female with left breast mass  reexcision of sentinel node biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROADENOMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 04 at 14 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left sentinel lymph node  is an irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue  Measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  A tan white lymphoid is identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Lymph node is bisected and submitted in cassette A with the adjacent fat  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left reexcision breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 3cm irregular portion of fiberfatty tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan ellipse of skin which has a central linear 2 0cm well healed surgical incision  A single stitch denotes the superior margin and two stitches denotes the medial margin  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the superior margin with green ink  and the inferior margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the medial margin to the lateral margin at 3 5mm intervals to reveal a 1 9cm cavity and a small amount of blood clot which is surrounded by soft  mottled  yellow tissue  The cavity is located 0 8cm from the inferior margin  1 7cm from the superior margin  1 5cm from the posterior margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  The remainder of the tissue consist predominantly of adipose tissue with a scant amount of soft  white fibrous tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fibrous nodule located 2 0cm medial to the biopsy cavity and is located at the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted as  B E  Sections of biopsy cavity medial to lateral  F  Fibrous nodule  G  Medial end of specimen  H  Lateral end of specimen  Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 MAY 99 ACCESSIONED ON  04 MAY 99 at 11 40 CLINICAL DATA  History of invasive DCIS  with DCIS at anterior margin at re excision                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  ANTERIOR MARGIN    RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 99 at 14 20                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  RT breast re exc ca  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm irregular fragment of breast tissue with a short stitch on the superior margin and along stitch on the lateral margin  An unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan skin ellipse is attached by thin strip of breast tissue to the anterior surface  The anterior surface is opened revealing a tan pink biopsy cavity wall that is focally hemorrhagic  Specimen is inked black and the lateral aspect is overinked blue  The cavity wall comes to 0 4cm from the anterior lateral margin and 0 5cm from the medial lateral margin  Representative sections are submitted from inferior to superior in A B with the following margins  A  complete cross section with additional red ink on medial B  anterior medial C  lateral D  medial The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable and representative sections are submitted in E F  with skin in E  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT ANTERIOR MARGIN   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 01 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma grade 3 with  margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL FOCI  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY CAVITY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic vessel and blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm skin ellipse and unremarkable nipple areolar complex  There is a suture designating the superior aspect  There is a 7 0cm horizontal  linear  well healed scar present 4 5cm superior to the nipple  The excised surface is inked black  with the anterior surface overinked red  Cross sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity 1 0cm beneath the skin  beneath the scar  and abutting the deep margin along a broad front  The biopsy cavity is lined by white fibrous tissue with a few fibrous strands extending into the adjacent fat  There is also fat necrosis surrounding the biopsy cavity site  Tissue away from the biopsy cavity is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  No discrete lesions are identified  Section code  A  Biopsy cavity with deep margin B F  Sections of biopsy cavity from inferior to superior G H  Representative sections of tissue away from biopsy cavity  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
