Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  MUCINOUS CARCINOMA  HYPOCELLULAR COLLOID TYPE   REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE MARGINS WITH BROAD FRONTS  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE TUMOR  PRESENT AT MARGINS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture marking the deep edge of the specimen  The specimen is inked as follows  deep margin inked blue  the remainder of the specimen is inked black  The specimen is incised to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm irregular firm white mass with mucinous areas  cystification and hemorrhage  The mass grossly abuts the inked resection margin opposite the deep edge of the specimen  The specimen is submitted in its entirely in A through F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of yellow fatty breast parenchyma  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable yellow fatty breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes G through M  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  SUTURE MARKS DEEP EDGE PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL MARGINS , Yes.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 23 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with microcalcifications on left breast mammogram  and a strong family history of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 OF 3  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  25    COMEDO TYPE  MULTIFOCAL  MICROCALCIFICATIONS ARE PRESENT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 9cm in greatest diameter  Tumor focally extends to an inked resection margin  Tumor is identified in one small blood vessel  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with needle localization and accompanying roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a round  irregular  firm  white  gritty nodule  0 9cm in greatest extent  located at the distal portion of the wire and 0 8cm from the closest inked margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  now submitted in A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in B through J  with the nodule in E  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BRESAT   report_end  , Yes.
