Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  09 AUG 95 at 12 00 CLINICAL DATA  36 year old women with calcifications on mammogram and family history of breast cancer  who is undergoing a needle biopsy of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  A SINGLE MICROSOPIC FOCUS   0 1CM   PRESENT LESS THAN 0 1CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MIXED COMEDO AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The single focus of invasive carcinoma consists of a few single malignant cells that infiltrates a microscopic area less than 0 1cm  slide D   The microscopic nature of the invasive component precludes an accurate assessment of tumor grade  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The ductal carcinoma in situ is present in 4 of 11 slides  Dr  Koerner concurs with the diagnosis  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 AUG 95 at 16 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through K  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT   NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Yes.
