ignature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left excisional biopsy  stitch long lateral  short superior   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm yellow fatty biopsy specimen with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm of attached fatty tissue on the inferior end  The surgeon has designated the lateral margin with a long stitch and the superior margin with a short stitch  The specimen contains one needle localization wire traversing the specimen in a lateral to medial direction  The long axis of the specimen is in the superior to inferior direction and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior aspect to reveal a poorly defined diffuse area of mild nodularity abutting the anterior  posterior  lateral and superior margins  coming to 0 3cm of the medial margin and approaching 0 5cm of the inferior margin  Sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Superior margin radially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inferior margin radially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire specimen from superior to inferior   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Attached fatty tissue serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral portions of the superior margin radially sectioned  Received fresh  labeled  left breast lumpectomy with needle localization   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm lumpectomy specimen  The surgeon designates the lateral margin with a long stitch  the superior margin with a short stitch  and the anterior margin with a clip  The long axis of the specimen is in the medial to lateral direction  Two localization wires are noted within the specimen traversing in a lateral to medial direction to orient the region of calcifications  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  and inferior   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral long axis to reveal an irregular tan to pink firm nodular area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm containing multiple areas of calcification and hemorrhage  The nodular area is 0 4cm from the lateral margin  3 8cm from the medial margin  0 5cm from the anterior margin  0 2cm from the posterior  0 1cm from the superior margin  and abuts the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  radially sectioned  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  radially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest posterior and inferior margins  inked black and yellow respectively   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to closest superior and anterior margins inked green and blue respectively   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of mass  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Some tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  461  to chromosome 17 signals  117  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  2  report_end  , Yes.
