 Breast  Right  block J   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  02 MAY 03 at 15 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of tan yellow fatty breast tissue with two localization wires in place  A black bow tie stitch designates superior  and a long black stitch lateral  and a short black stitch anterior  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the lateral green and the medial yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm hemorrhagic cavity with dark red blood clot  which comes to 0 5cm of the anterior  0 3cm of the medial  1 7cm of the posterior  2 6cm of the lateral  1 9cm of the superior  and  5 0cm of the inferior margins  Adjacent to the cavity are minimal yellow orange foci consistent with fat necrosis  The surrounding fibrous tissue is focally nodular  predominantly surrounding the tip of the localization wire along the most superoanterior aspect of the specimen  The remaining cut surface is unremarkable and representative sections are submitted from inferior to superior as A J with the cavity as D H  and the tissue designated by the localization wire as I J  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  JHE                                              