ive components  helping to excluding concomitant lobular carcinoma  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple nodules  The largest measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  slide measurement   Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to   0 05cm from the posterior margin of the specimen in one focus in the lateral most breast  and is 0 1cm from the anterior margin in one focus  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Grade of ductal carcinoma in situ  1 and REMOVED_DATE Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to   0 02cm from the anterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  Stains for receptors  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Her 2 Only   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  INCLUDING SENTINEL NODES  TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  17 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   1 Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  hot and blue   is a fibrofatty specimen with three lymph nodes identified  Each lymph node is bisected and frozen as FX 1  FX 1A and FX 1B  finally submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node nonsentinel 385   are two fragments of fibrofatty tissue and potential lymph node  submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s na