Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 51 CLINICAL DATA  Abundant calcifications on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  THREE FOCI OF MINIMALLY INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 05 CM  REMOVED_DATE CM  AND REMOVED_DATE CM MAXIMUM DIMENSION ON TISSUE SECTIONS   SEE NOTE  2  WIDESPREAD DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING INTO MANY LOBULES AND AREAS OF SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND PRESENT AT MULTIPLE RESECTION MARGINS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The entire specimen has been submitted for histological evaluation  No definite lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is demonstrated  Estrogen and progesterone receptor stains will be performed on sections of one of the larger foci of invasion  slide C  and the results reported as an addendum  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 43 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE INFILTRATING TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE INFILTRATING TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tissue with focal areas of gritty calcification  An accompanying specimen xray show abundant calcifications  A representative section of the gritty  calcified tissue is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder submitted in B R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , Yes.
