Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left mastectomy with stitch at 12 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  MULTICENTRIC INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1  2  EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  At least 4 foci  measuring 0 7cm  0 6cm  0 15cm  and  0 1cm  located in the lower outer  anterolateral  upper inner  and central inferior regions of the breast  respectively  See note  GRADE  1  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Indeterminate  See note  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to  0 1cm from the anterior margin in one focus in the lateral breast  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  present in multiple quadrants  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1 to focal 2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Positive at the anterior margin of the specimen in the lower outer quadrant  Ductal carcinoma in situ is also  0 1cm from the anterior margin in several other foci in the lateral breast and the central inferior breast  and comes to 0 17cm from the posterior margin in one focus in the lower outer quadrant  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Additional foci of early invasive papillary carcinoma cannot be entirely excluded in regions of myoepithelial cell loss associated with ductal carcinoma in situ  immunostains for calponin  SM MHC  and p63 were evaluated  Tumor is noted within lymphatic vessels in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Although much of this intralymphatic tumor has a fragmented and folded appearance suggestive of artifactual displacement  the possibility of focal genuine lymphatic invasion cannot be entirely excluded  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSCTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   RE EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are three containers which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm axillary tail  A black stitch designates the 12 o clock aspect  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan pink unremarkable nipple which comes to 0 5cm of the superior skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  gray white fibrous scar with an eccentric  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm hemorrhagic focus  The scar abuts the anterior and posterior margins along the inferolateral aspect of the breast  Located 0 3cm lateral to this area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm poorly delineated  firm  nodular  tan pink lesion  which come to 0 2cm of the posterior and 0 1cm of the anterior margins  There are several suspicious tan red nodular areas immediately posterior to the scar  which occupy a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm area and range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  The nodules come to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  The nodules are diffuse and are also located in patches throughout the remaining mammary tissue  One of these patches measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and is located in the subareolar anterolateral breast tissue  This area focally abuts the anterior margin  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals several possible tan pink lymph nodes averaging 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Subareolar anterolateral breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mid lower  central inferior  breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scar  lower outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between scar and nodular area in lower outer breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area in lower outer breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from axillary tail which may represent lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  axillary contents left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three intact lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  final lateral margin left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan pink  fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along one aspect designating the new margin  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal hemorrhage and dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast re excision skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink skin ellipse  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  The margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   E