argins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The results will be reported in an addendum  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  1  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN EIGHTEEN LYMPH NODES  0 18   SEE NOTE   2  AXILLARY HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  No lymphovascular invasion is present  Post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Sataloff Grading  N B  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm oriented breast tissue with 2 needle localization wires in place  an accompanying radiograph  a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral margin of the specimen  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green and lateral   yellow  Upon sectioning  the breast parenchyma consists predominantly of dense pink white fibrous stroma with a moderate amount of fatty tissue  The breast parenchyma between the 2 needle localization wires shows 3 metallic clips  small foci of fat necrosis and a tan pink tumor bed measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  which abuts the posterior and lateral margins of the specimen  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the superior end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the inferior end margin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the region denoted by the 2 needle localization wires  with clips and the entire tumor bed  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is dissected and palpated to reveal 18 lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimensions  An ill defined healing biopsy site is present  All lymph nodes are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows   