Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 19 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  FOCAL MICROSCOPIC INFILTRATING AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  RESIDUAL IN BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The focus of residual invasive carcinoma is approximately REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  in cross section  Adjacent to this area are small foci of solid  and cribiform type ductal carcinoma in situ  The resection margins are free of tumor  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 13                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a 30 x 16 x 3cm right modified mastectomy specimen including an 8 x 5 x 1cm tail of adipose and 24 x 11cm skin ellipse  The skin ellipse contains a nipple and 3 5cm well healed scar just superior to the nipple  The remaining skin is intact and unremarkable  with two 0 2cm in diameter  flat  bright red lesions present  both inferior and superior to the nipple  The excisional margins are inked  Beneath the biopsy site is a confluent  non cystic area of firm  tan white to red yellow tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  At a distance of 2cm from this firm fibrous area there is a 2 2cm in diameter  thin walled cyst filled with dark brown soft material  The cyst wall is 0 1cm in thickness  This hematoma site is not in obvious continuity with the firm tissue beneath the biopsy site  Surrounding this probable biopsy site cystic cavity is an area of tan gray tissue with focal linear streaking into the surrounding adipose  This area of firm tissue is REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and is somewhat similar in appearance to the tissue immediately beneath the biopsy site  This focus  however  is not in continuity with the biopsy site  and extends to within 1 5cm of the nearest margin  which is deep and slightly superior  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed mostly of adipose  with fine white  linear streaking  no other masses and no other cysts  The axillary tail contains multiple firm  tan white nodules which may represent lymph node  measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in length  the larger lymph nodes with fatty replacement  Section Code A   nipple and red skin lesion B C   skin with biopsy site and underlying firm tissue D G   hematoma site with surrounding tissue and nearest margin H J   representative breast parenchyma including all quadrants K O   lymph nodes Resident  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  OR ROOM UNKNOWN REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    report_end  , Checked.
