Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 59 CLINICAL DATA  Patient status post infiltrating lobular carcinoma of the left breast  previous biopsy on right breast  focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia and atypical lobular hyperplasia                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA WITH FOCAL PAGETOID SPREAD  2  INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MULTIFOCAL  WITH FOCAL CYTOLOGIC ATYPIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  4  FIBROADENOMA  SMALL  5  SMALL FOCUS OF COLLAGENOUS SPHERULOSIS  SECTION I   6  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE MATERIAL  CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The fibrocystic change also includes sclerosing adenosis  microcyst formation  apocrine metaplasia and fibrosis  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 08 Staff Pathologist  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received labeled  Right breast  is a 25 x 14 x 3cm right mastectomy specimen with an overlying 15 x 7cm skin ellipse that contains 1cm in diameter nipple  There is a partially healed 1 5cm scar  1cm superolaterally to the nipple  The specimen is inked and seriallly sectioned to reveal a 4 x 2cm tan  variegated  firm mass with focal hemorrhaged areas  The mass is centrally located in the region of the biopsy cavity and extends to within 0 5cm from the deep inked resection margin  2cm from the superior resection margin  2cm from the inferior resection margin  and is within 0 5cm from the skin  There are two separate tan white nodular areas noted away from the biopsy cavity  One nodule is tan white measures 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and is 3cm lateral to 