ecimen  with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm ellipse of skin is notable for a 4 5cm linear  well healed scar at the lateral aspect  The nipple and areola appear unremarkable  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm biopsy cavity  which is present in the central to outer aspect of the specimen and is exposed at the posterior surface  The cavity extends to 3 5cm of the anterior margin  The cavity has a slightly nodular tan pink to gray white lining  The surrounding tissue is lobulated  tan yellow to focally hemorrhagic and fibrofatty  No other abnormalities are identified  Lymph nodes are not detected in the lateral tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of biopsy cavity and surrounding tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections away from the biopsy cavity  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast skin   are 2 pieces of white skin  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  FX 1A   FX 1B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  THERE IS A MONOTONOUS LYMPHOCYTIC POPULATION THAT WILL BE CHARACTERIZED ON PERMANENTS AND MAY BE CONSISTENT WITH PATIENT S KNOWN CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 18   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 19 38PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART C  Skin  Right Breast   Excision PART D  Cryostat Frozen Section  sl