affin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four parts  Labeled  left breast lump  is breast tissue with a small skin ellipse and a biopsy cavity  After the margins are inked black  one slice near the medial aspect  not the actual margin  is frozen as frozen section  1  now submitted as A  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm fragment of breast has attached black sutures designated as  short suture superior  long suture lateral   The superior aspect is inked green  over black ink   The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm tan white  ill defined stellate mass  which grossly extends to the superior  superficial  deep and medial margins  A representative section of the mass where it abuts the superior superficial and deep margins is submitted in B  The most medial margin is taken en face  breadloafed and submitted entirely in C  Two other representative sections 