Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is note seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  MINIMAL  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  16  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 10                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of breast with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm firm  gritty  tan  lobulated mass  The tumor comes less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin  1 5cm from the superior margin  1 2cm from the inferior margin  and 1 0cm from the posterior margin  The remainder of the specimen consists of white  rubbery adipose tissue  The specimen is submitted as follows  A B   tumor in relation to the anterior margin  C D   tumor  E   superior margin  F   posterior margin  G   medial margin  H   lateral margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  Labeled  additional superficial margin L breast mass  are two fragments of fatty and dense white tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm in aggregate  sectioned in cassette I  Labeled  final shaved margins L breast margin  are multiple fragments of dense white and focally fatty tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  submitted entirely in J O  Labeled  L axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm fatty fragment with multiple small unremarkable lymph nodes of up to 1 3cm  in cassettes P R  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   TUMOR LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Di