Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 30 CLINICAL DATA  Increasing calcifications on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   20    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  80   CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPES  MULTIFOCAL AND PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Estrogen receptors will be reported in an addendum     FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES     INTRAPARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODES  2  NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm red and yellow breast tissue fragment with a localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 4cm tan  firm  rubbery to gritty central region with faintly retracted borders  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through I  with the tan central region in A through D  Gross Description by  Douglas B  Flieder  MD Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND A MINUTE FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR    0 4CM   TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Yes.
