Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 59 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  TOTAL MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  MARKED SCAR LIKE FIBROSIS  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  MONKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 42                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm mastectomy specimen with a long stitch indicating lateral  and a short stitch indicating the anterior margin of the previous axillary dissection  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm skin ellipse with a 4 8cm well healed scar  approximately 2 5cm away from a grossly unremarkable nipple  and a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm portion of skeletal muscle at the deep soft tissue resection margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  white lobulated mass with a glistening smooth cut surface  and a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm cystic cavity lined with tan brown fibrinous exudate and focal hemorrhage  The mass comes to within 0 4cm of the deep margin  0 5cm of the closest overlying skin and is grossly far away from the lateral and medial soft tissue resection margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is notable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cystic cavity lined by a fibrous wall with a smooth tan to brown glistening inner surface  located at the short stitch  designated anterior margin of old axillary dissection   Surrounding this area is more firm indurated breast parenchyma with areas of hemorrhage  The remaining parenchyma shows fibrofatty tissue  The nipple is unremarkable  Section code  A  biopsy cavity  deep margin B G  representative sections of biopsy cavity and surrounding firm white mass H  representative section of biopsy cavity in relation to overlying skin I  representative section of more fibrous breast away from biopsy cavity  J M  representative sections of tissue in area of glistening membrane adjacent to anterior margin of old axillary dissection  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 27 CLINICAL DATA  85 y o  female with left breast mass  R O carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE CORE BIOPSIES  B CELL LYMPHOMA CONSISTENT WITH EXTRANODAL MARGINAL ZONE B CELL LYMPHOMA OF MUCOSA ASSOCIATED LYMPHOID TISSUE  MALT  TYPE  NOTE  There is a dense lymphoid infiltrate with focal reactive gemmal centers and a diffuse infiltrate of monomorphous small round lymphocytes  Focally  there are medium sized  irregular cells consistent with marginal zone cells  The differential diagnosis includes small lymphocytic lymphoma  follicle center lymphoma  mantle cell lymphoma and MALT type lymphoma  Immunoperoxidase stains show a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   phenotype consistent with MALT type lymphoma  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 39                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin heavy and light chains there is high background  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stain shows large irregular follicular dendritic cell meshworks  Similar staining is seen with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to bcl 2 tumor cells are positive and germinal centers are negative  The cells are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of extranodal marginal zone B cell lymphoma and tend to exclude mantle cell  follicular and small lymphocytic lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  are 9 cores of yellow pink fibroadipose tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto to cassette A  Gross Description by  Robert F Donnell Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Gerald Joseph Doyle  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY , Unchecked.
