ure below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink lymph node with attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right axillary non sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular portion of glistening yellow lobulated lymph node bearing adipose tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm well circumscribed rubbery tan pink possible lymph node is identified  The lymph node is trisected and submitted in entirety labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 16 x 3 2cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The specimen is partially surfaced by a 24 x 8 5cm elliptical portion of wrinkled tan skin  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm well healed scar and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  and the specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic defect located in the mid inferior aspect of the specimen subjacent to the skin scar and coming within 0 5cm of the posterior margin  This defect is consistent with a previous biopsy site  The tissue surrounding the defect is dense rubbery tan white fibrous tissue with focal areas of hemorrhage and fat necrosis  No lesions or masses are identified  The remaining cut surfaces reveal multiple blue black nodules that are filled with red brown hemorrhagic substance which range from 0 2cm to 0 5cm in diameter  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of defect sequentially from medial to lateral to include closest deep margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved breast parenchyma  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  101  to chromosome 17 signals  97  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOV