Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA  Breast and nipple biopsy    Paget s disease                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN IN SEVERAL AREAS  AND FOCALLY INTO THE DERMIS OF THE OVERLYING SKIN  LYMPHATIC INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5   NOTE  Paget s disease is not seen  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   13  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical 