Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 54 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma on biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  ADJACENT TO AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY SITE  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  LACTATIONAL CHANGES  5  ALL  22  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Note  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of resection appear free of invasive and in situ carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  One specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  stitch marks superior aspect  and consists of a 23 x 14 x 3cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with a stitch marking the superior aspect and containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm irregular skin ellipse containing a nipple and a 2 5cm curvilinear scar  7 2cm lateral to the nipple  The specimen is inked and cross sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm hard mass beneath the scar  with an inhomogeneous tan yellow  cystic and brown cut surface  and abutting the anterior skin  The mass is greater than 1 5cm from the deep margin  Sections of the tumor are submitted in A through E  from medial to lateral  with B and C containing anterior superior margins and D and E containing anterior margins  There is 4 x 2 x 2cm area inferior and lateral to the mass which is firm and gray white  and abutting the inferior  anterior margin  Representative sections in F and G  1 5cm medial to the tumor is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm firm  white area  1 2cm from the nearest margin  anterior   Representative section is in H  Sectioning the tissue away from the mass reveals unremarkable fatty and white soft parenchyma  Representative sections are in I and J  with J in the area of the nipple  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  which are submitted in K through U  Please note that M contains a single node  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  18 AUG 98 at 11 36 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old status post right lumpectomy in  95  Now presents with right breast lump with palpable nodes and suspicious lesions in the left breast  The patient had four cycles of adryamycin and Taxol                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SEVERAL NODULES AGGREGATING TO ABOUT 1 CM OR LESS AND PRESENT AT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SMALL FOCI  RADIAL SCARS  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN FIVE OF FORTY NINE LYMPH NODES WITH SLIGHT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH CALCIFICATIONS  RADIAL SCARS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  26 AUG 98 at 16 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm with an axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is attached to an ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm which includes the nipple  The nipple displays a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white nodule 4 5cm lateral to the nipple there is a puckered indentation  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a poorly circumscribed fibrous lesion that appears to extend to the deep margin of resection in a region designated by the surgeon with a stitch  This area corresponds to the puckered lesion on the skin s surface  An accurate measurement of this area cannot be given due to poor circumscription and diffuse fibrosis surrounding the lesion  Dissection of the axillary tail reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to up to 0 9cm in largest dimension  Section code  A F  Lymph nodes  G  Lesion to deep margin  H I  Lesion including skin  puckered area  and deep margin J K L  Additional sections of fibrous region M  Nipple with white nodule  T X  Additional sections  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a simple mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The overlying ellipse of skin  including the nipple  is unremarkable and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal diffusely fibrotic breast parenchyma  One focal lesion is identified in the subareola region consisting of a poorly defined firm area within the fibrotic breast parenchyma spanning approximately 1 5cm in largest dimension  This area is located approximately 0 8cm from the deep margin of resection  Sections are taken as follows  Section code  N O  Suspicious focus  entirely submitted  cassette N  lesion to deep margin   P S  Representative sections of fibrotic breast parenchyma  Y CC  Additional sections Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No.
