pecimen   STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Note  To evaluate for invasive carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  calponin  smooth muscle myosin heavy chain  p63  and cytokeratin were examined  on each of 2 blocks  the findings support the above diagnosis   Immunohistochemical staining including cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE  cytokeratin 14   E Cadherin  on two blocks  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  have been examined  Selected slides were  reviewed with Dr  M  Lerwill who concurs with the above diagnosis     LYMPH NODE  LEFT   SENTINEL    EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1      NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on levels  from each of two blocks  The findings support the above diagnosis     LYMPH NODE  LEFT   SENTINEL    EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  0 1      NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on tissue  levels  The findings support the above diagnosis       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab are 2 specimens  both labeled Nancy  Smith  REMOVE_MRN     Labeled  left sentinel node   is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node frozen entirely  as FX 1 and attached adipose tissue  not frozen   The lymph node is now  submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining adipose tissue is submitted in  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Labeled  left sentinel node  87   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lymph node bivalved  and entirely frozen as FX 2  now submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left mastectomy   is a 20  x REMOVED_DATE x 4cm mastectomy specimen  with a suture designating the axillary tail   There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm skin ellipse that has a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm brown  nodule in the medial aspect  0 6cm from the closest skin margin  The areola  appears unremarkable  the nipple is retracted  The anterior margin is inked  blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x  1 2 x 0 6cm tan  firm stellate nodule in the upper inner quadrant at  approximately 2 o clock  This nodule is located 0 9cm from the posterior  margin and 1 2cm from the anterior margin and is referred to as mass  1  REMOVED_DATE  cm inferior to mass  1 and extending laterally is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 1 6cm irregular  nodular lesion  this will now be referred to as mass  2  which appears to  extend along the fibrous bands  Mass  2 extends 7 slices lateral of mass  1   Mass  2 is 0 5cm from the anterior margin and is adjacent to the posterior  margin  It appears to extend into the nipple  In addition  there is a 0 3cm  in diameter firm nodule at 12 o clock  located 0 6cm from the anterior margin   2 5cm from the posterior margin  and 2 5cm from mass  2  The remainder of  the breast parenchyma is unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  No lymph nodes are  identified in the lateral most portion  Representative sections are submitted  as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to closest anterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  1 to closest posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section mass  1 to posterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section just inferior to mass  1  intervening section between mass  1 to  mass  2     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass  2 from 1st slice adjacent to slice  containing both mass  1 and mass  2    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass  2 from 2nd slice    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from 3rd slice   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains representative  sections of   papillary involvement   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains