ATED BY A SUTURE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  A cytokeratin stain performed on a deeper tissue section does not show the tumor cells and is noncontributory  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast biopsy  needle localization   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm breast excision specimen with a long stitch marking its medial edge and a short stitch marking its inferior edge  There is a single needle localization wire in the specimen identifying a clip from a prior biopsy  The long axis of the specimen is medial to lateral and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis to reveal focally firm breast parenchyma with focal hemorrhage in the area of the needle localization wire  The clip is identified adjacent to this area of hemorrhage  The clip is located 0 5cm from the posterior margin  and 0 3cm from the superior margin  The clip is located greater than 1 0cm from all other margins  The section containing the clip  removed  is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Adjacent sections of the biopsy site and needle localization wire are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections of the lateral margin including grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Radial sections of the medial resection margin  including grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary content   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary node dissection specimen  The specimen is dissected to reveal scar tissue and a few potential lymph nodes  which are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional putative lymph nodes are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final inferior margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm breast shave tissue with a single stitch marking the new margin  The new margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final deep margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast tissue specimen with a single stitch marking the new margin  The new margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final superior hemisphere   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm breast excision specimen with a short stitch marking its new superior margin and a long stitch marking its new medial margin  The long axis of the specimen is medial to lateral and the entire inferior surface is cauterized  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to demonstrate grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General H