 margin  There are two recent incisions  tied closed with suture material  The first is radially oriented starting just lateral to the areola and is 2 0cm in length  The second is circumferentially oriented and is 2 0cm superior and lateral to the areola  The deep surface of the breast specimen consists of fascia with attached strips of muscle up to 0 5cm in thickness  There is an attached 10 x 5 x 2 3cm axillary tail  Underneath the lateral  radially oriented scar  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm blood and clot filled biopsy cavity  biopsy cavity  A    Underneath the superior  lateral  circumferential skin incision is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm blood and clot filled biopsy cavity  biopsy cavity B   Biopsy cavity A is 1 4cm from the closest deep margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of firmness between biopsy cavities A and B  On the medial side of biopsy cavity A there is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  stellate  fibrous region which is located beneath the nipple  Cheesy  white material can be seen filling dilated ducts beneath the nipple  White  fibrous tendrils emanate from this area and extend to the inferior resection margin  Biopsy cavity B is 0 2cm from the closest deep resection margin  On the medial portion of biopsy cavity B is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  firm  stellate  tan white mass  region C  which is 2 0cm from the nearest deep margin and 1 1cm from the nearest superior margin  This region is just superior to the area described underneath the nipple  Sixteen axillary lymph nodes are identified  two are grossly positive  Section Code  A   deep margin  biopsy cavity A B D   inferior margins from area underneath nipple taken radially E   area between biopsy cavities A and B F G   representative area underneath nipple H   deep margin  radial biopsy cavity B I   representative area C J   closest extent of region C to superior margin K   representative area of breast from medial portion of mastectomy specimen L   nipple M R   axillary nodes Resident  James Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Robert Carl Hagberg  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
