surface of the specimen  therefore the anterior surface is not inked  The posterior is inked black  the superior is inked green and the inferior is inked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm hard  leathery  tan light brown mass in the subareolar area  The center of the mass corresponds to the biopsy site  which is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The mass appears to abut the posterior resection margin  it is roughly 5 0cm from the inferior resection margin  6 0cm from the superior margin and focally extends to the skin surface but does not appear to involve the skin resection margins  Four representative sections of the lesion with the posterior resection margin are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved breast with the inferior resection margin closest to the lesion is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the uninvolved breast with superior margin closest to lesion submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The attached axillary tissue was dissected for lymph nodes  Several potential lymph nodes were identified and submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node quadrisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for pr