yma is unremarkable  Dissection through the axillary tail reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging from 0 3cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Section code  A B  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest deep margin C  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest overlying skin D E  Biopsy cavity with surrounded  indurated tissue F  Firm focus of fibrous tissue adjacent to biopsy cavity G I  Representative of each lymph node  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  51   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  PAC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 14 09  Results To   Kevin S  Hughes MD  Chien Wei Eric Liao MD  PhD    FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT     Invasive ductal carcinoma with extensive dermal involvement     Metastatic carcinoma in 10 of 11 axillary lymph nodes and multinodular  axillary soft tissue involvement     Ductal carcinoma in situ with calcifications     Fibrocystic changes and sclerosing adenosis with calcifications     Focal areas of fibrosis in parenchyma  skin  and lymph nodes consistent with  therapy effect     See note and tables  1 and  2     NOTE  Although focal areas of fibrosis consistent with therapy effect are  present  there is abundant residual invasive carcinoma both in the parenchyma  and skin  The overall grade is 2  tubule formation   2  nuclear pleomorphism    2  mitotic activity   3   but this does not quite reflect the morphologic  heterogeneity that is present  This heterogeneity is represented by many areas  that appear grade 1  some areas that appear grade 2  and scattered areas with  poor tubule formation and high mitotic activity  which would warrant a grade of  3 if viewed in isolation  Focal tumoral necrosis and minor extracellular mucin  production are also noted       TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA    Tumor Size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with multiple subcentimeter satellite nodules   Grade  2  see note above    Lymphatic Vessel Invasion  Suspicious for a focus of dermal lymphatic invasion   Blood Vessel Invasion  Not identified   Perineural Invasion  Present   Margin of Invasive Carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma comes to 0 15cm from the  medial skin margin in one focus  The remaining skin margins and parenchymal  margins are  0 2cm away   Location of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  Within the region of the mass   Grade of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  2 to focal 3   Margin of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm  or greater   Stains for Receptors  Requested       TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2  SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES    Total Number of Positive Lymph Nodes  10  Total Number of Lymph Nodes Examined  11    Number with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0    Number with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   2    Number with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   8  Extracapsular Extension  Marked   Other Forms of Axillary Involvement  Lymphatic vessels and multifocal soft  tissue metastases              Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD         PROCEDURES ADDENDA  Hormone Receptor Quantitation    QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note       Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining o