r breast tissue  which is located 2 2cm of the posterior margin  No axillary lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Stellate scar and surrounding dense fibrous tissue of the lower inner quadrant  including the closest inked margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Suspicious fibrous tissue of the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional fibrous tissue including the mid outer quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent axillary lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan irregular  unremarkable skin  excised to a depth of 0 3cm  A discrete lesion is not identified  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Amendment  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain   1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete m