 identified in the 6 5cm fibrotic region represent confluent ductal carcinoma in situ  Multiple levels examined  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE SUMMARY IN TABLE  2  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 32 LYMPH NODES  SEE SUMMARY IN TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  33 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   1  sentinel   Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan gray to pink  slightly firm soft tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1 and  1A  which are now resubmitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  respectively  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast stitch at axillary tail   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm right mastectomy specimen with a black stitch designating the axillary tail  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm ellipse of tan pink skin with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm prominent tan pink nipple which comes to 0 5cm of the inferomedial skin margin  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm indurated gray pink tumor mass at approximately the 12 o clock position which comes to  0 1cm from the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  Located 3 0cm inferior and lateral to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm area of dense gray white fibrous tissue with indurated tan pink tumor masses throughout ranging from REMOVED_DATE to roughly 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The tumor masses occupy approximately 80  of this dense fibrous region  This area comes to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  Adjacent to this region along the medial aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan yellow serous fluid filled cyst with a smooth  glistening gray white fibrous lining measuring 0 1cm in thickness  The cyst wall comes to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  Located 2 0cm superior to the cyst  3 0cm medial to the dense gray white fibrous mass and 1 5cm inferomedial to the first mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm indurated gray pink nodule which comes to 0 4cm of the posterior margin  Sectioning of the axillary region reveals several tan red possible lymph nodes averaging 0 4cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest tumor mass submitted from lateral to medial with posterior margins in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Well defined tumor mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cyst to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial most  smallest tumor mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple possible lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of tan pink fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal multiple tan red lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 1cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  One of the lymph nodes is inked and bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  One of the lymph nodes is inked black and serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm tan white irregular  unoriented portion of skin excised to a depth of 0 4cm  The epidermis displays a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan gray bean shaped lesion  which comes to within 0 1cm of the margin  The margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned  Also received in the same container  are three tan white thin fragments of skin ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional fragments of skin  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND  1A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Melinda J Lerwill M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c er