d as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire tan white fibrous area  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Inner breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant tissue that may represent possible nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the lateral margin  The overlying tan brown skin measures REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm and contains a 3 0cm curved scar between the 12 and 3 o clock position that lies 2 5cm from the nipple  A second 4 5cm linear scar is present at 4 o clock  5 0cm from the nipple  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two tan white  fibrous  stellate shaped scars  The first scar measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and lies in the central region approximately beneath the curved scar present between the 12 and 3 o clock position on the overlying skin  It lies 2 0cm from the overlying skin and 5 5cm from the posterior inked surface  The second scar measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and lies in the lower outer quadrant beneath the linear scar at the 4 o clock position and lies 1 5cm from the overlying skin and 6 0cm from the posterior inked surface  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows diffuse tan white fibrous tissue and small cystic spaces filled with blue fluid  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire first scar located in the central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin closest to the first scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire second stellate scar located in the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Posterior margin closest to the second scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper o