Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 53 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  8 CM  EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY   METASTATIC CARCINOMA INVOLVING 19 OF 23 LYMPH NODES AND EXTENDING INTO AXILLARY FAT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  Some of the metastases in the lymph nodes span less than 0 2cm  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estsrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast with axillary contents  is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm  with an axillary tail that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  and a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm  The nipple is slightly off center located at 11 0cm from the medial end of the skin ellipse  A firm mass is palpable directly below the nipple  The specimen is inked and serial sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm irregular shaped  firm  white mass within the specimen that extends to approximately 1 5cm from a deep resection margin  posterior margin   Fibrous tissue also extends from the mass to within 0 5cm of the inferior resection margin  Section code  A  lateral end of the tumor mass B  representative section from the inferior portion of the tumor C  a section of the tumor near the center of the mass D  a section of the tumor medial and inferior that in section C E  a section of the medial end of the tumor mass Approximately 23 lymph nodes or fragments of lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail  Two of the largest ones measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Nine medium sized lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in the largest diameter  The remainder are smaller than 0 5cm in their largest dimension  These lymph nodes are submitted in cassette F J  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   repo