ck  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  The ductal carcinoma in situ shows a morphological spectrum including cribriform  papillary and solid types  the nuclear grade ranging from low and intermediate to high grade with comedonecrosis  Ductal carcinoma in situ is located in the vicinity of the invasive carcinoma and healing biopsy site  and away from the lesion  Invasive carcinoma and healing biopsy site appear grossly coalescent as one mass lesion  Immunohistochemical stains  p63  myosin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   show myoepithelial cells surrounding ductal carcinoma in situ but do not confirm carcinoma in lymphatic vessels  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  SEE TABLE  2  NOTE  The metastatic deposit in the sentinel lymph node measures 1 5cm and consists of high grade invasive ductal carcinoma  replacing the lymph node parenchyma nearly in its entirety  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  A cytokeratin stain is positive  which supports the diagnosis  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA IN THE BACKGROUND OF FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL PROLIFERATION  FAVOR LOW GRADE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM AWAY FROM THE NEW  INKED MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The atypical ductal proliferation is negative for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE by immunohistochemistry  Multiple levels examined   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN DEEP   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN ONE SMALL LYMPH NODE  0 1    SEE NOTE   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL PROLIFERATION  FAVOR LOW GRADE SOLID TYPE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOC