erior and inferior margins  E H  Additional sections range from medial to lateral including nodular areas in all sections  I  One axillary lymph node  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm    quadrasected  J  One axillary lymph node  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm    bisected  K  One axillary lymph node  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm    bisected  L  One axillary lymph node  1 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5   bisected  M  Four axillary lymph nodes  0 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm    whole  N  Two axillary lymph nodes  1 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE    whole  O  Axillary cyst  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9   quadrasected  P Y Additional breast tissue sections  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   LYMPH NODE LEFT A , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  30 MAY 96 at 11 04 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  30    GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM IN DIAMETER MEASURED FROM SLIDES  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  70    LOW GRADE  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  HARBORING ABUNDANT MICROCALCIFICATIONS  EXTENDING WELL AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR  SPANNING A REGION REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION MEASURED FROM SLIDES  A FULL SECTION WIDTH   AND EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 